      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>Three weeks after an inspection app goes live, use slides. By month three the forms are filled in at the site office, not where the hazards are. That is friction, not laziness.</p><p>Here is what a UK site safety inspection must cover, a template, and a way to get it done on site.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>CDM 2015</strong> needs inspections by a competent person. The format is not set. The record must show what was checked.</li><li>The real problem is finishing on site, not from memory.</li><li>Tools that need a login or install get finished less often than tools people already use.</li><li>A dated photo beats a tidy form with nothing behind it.</li><li><strong>RIDDOR</strong> reporting applies to certain incidents. It is separate from the inspection record.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The job",
      "heading": "What a site safety inspection covers",
      "html": "<p>It is a walk round a site to find hazards, test controls and record what you find. You check that the site matches the risk assessment and method statements.</p><p>Under CDM 2015 the principal contractor must monitor construction phase health and safety. Regular inspections show it. A form filled in from memory proves only that the form was filled in.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The record",
      "heading": "What the report must include",
      "html": "<p>The law sets no fixed format. The record must show a competent person visited and logged what they found. At least:</p><ul><li>Site name and address</li><li>Date and time</li><li>Your name and role</li><li>Weather</li><li>Number of workers on site</li><li>What you checked and its condition</li><li>Hazards found</li><li>Actions, who and by when</li><li>Your signature</li></ul><p>Dated photos make it much stronger. A note about defective scaffold boarding at grid C3, with a photo, stands up.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The template",
      "heading": "Free site safety inspection checklist",
      "html": "<p>Items for a standard walk round.</p><p><strong>Access and egress.</strong> Entrances and exits clear and signed. Walkways separate from plant. Emergency routes clear.</p><p><strong>Working at height.</strong> Scaffold, ties, boards, guard rails, toe boards. Ladders footed and tied. MEWPs and operators. Edge protection.</p><p><strong>Plant.</strong> Inspection records current. Operators competent. Exclusion zones held.</p><p><strong>Welfare.</strong> Toilets, washing, eating area, first aid.</p><p><strong>Housekeeping, PPE, fire.</strong> Tidy site. COSHH stored right. PPE worn. Extinguishers in date. Hot works permits.</p><p><strong>Paperwork.</strong> Construction phase plan to hand. RAMS current. Any RIDDOR incidents since last time.</p>"
    },
    {
