      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What must a site safety inspection report include under CDM 2015?</h3><p>CDM 2015 needs inspections by a competent person. Record the site, date and time, who inspected, what was checked, what was found and any action. Check current HSE guidance for your work.</p><h3>How often are site safety inspections needed?</h3><p>It depends on the work and risk. Scaffold must be inspected before first use, after any event that may affect it, and at least every seven days. General site inspections are often weekly. The principal contractor's risk assessment sets it.</p><h3>Can I do a site safety inspection on a phone?</h3><p>Yes. What matters is doing it on site, during the inspection, not afterwards. WhatsApp has nothing to install and no login.</p><h3>Who can carry out a CDM site safety inspection?</h3><p>A competent person. That means someone with enough knowledge of the hazards on that site. Check current HSE guidance.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/near-miss-reporting-construction-uk.html\">Near miss reporting in construction</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/risk-assessment-software-uk-sme.html\">Risk assessment software for UK SMEs</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/h-and-s-site-walkround-checklist-uk.html\">H&S site walkround checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/coshh-risk-assessment-field-teams-uk.html\">COSHH risk assessment for field teams</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">Quickler works in any country</a></li></ul>"
